    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt;, n = 0 - 3</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Trace External Input Select Register &lt;n&gt;</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>Use this to set, or read, which External Inputs are resources to the trace unit.</p>

      
        <p>The name TRCEXTINSELR is an alias of TRCEXTINSELR0.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>External register TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt; bits [31:0] are architecturally mapped to AArch64 System register <a href="AArch64-trcextinselrn.html">TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt;[31:0]</a>.</p><p>This register is present only when FEAT_ETE is implemented and FEAT_TRC_EXT is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt; are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p><h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt; is a 32-bit register.</p>
      <h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_16">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-15_0">evtCount</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_16">Bits [31:16]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-15_0">evtCount, bits [15:0]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>PMU event to select.</p>
<p>Software must program this field with a PMU event that is supported by the PE being programmed.</p>
<p>If <span class="xref">FEAT_PMUv3p8</span> is implemented and this field is programmed to an event that is reserved or not supported by the PE, Arm recommends that the External Input Selector is not active and the value returned by a direct or external read of this field is the value written to the field.</p>
<p>Otherwise, if evtCount is programmed to a PMU event that is reserved or not supported by the PE, the behavior depends on the value written:</p>
<ul>
<li>For the range <span class="hexnumber">0x0000</span> to <span class="hexnumber">0x003F</span>, the External Input Selector is not active, and the value returned by a direct or external read of this field is the value written to the field.
</li><li>If <span class="xref">FEAT_PMUv3p1</span> is implemented, for the range <span class="hexnumber">0x4000</span> to <span class="hexnumber">0x403F</span>, Arm recommends that the External Input Selector is not active and the value returned by a direct or external read of this field is the value written to the field.
</li><li>For other values, it is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNPREDICTABLE</span> whether the External Input Selector is active and the value returned by a direct or external read of this field is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span>.
</li></ul><p><span class="arm-defined-word">UNPREDICTABLE</span> means the PMU event must not expose privileged information.</p>
<p>Arm recommends that the behavior across a family of implementations is defined such that if a given implementation does not include a PMU event from a set of common <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span> PMU events, then the External Input Selector is not active and the value read back on evtCount is the value written.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a Trace unit reset, 
      this field resets
       to an architecturally <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h2>Accessing TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt;</h2>
        <p>Must be programmed if any of the following is true: <a href="ext-trcrsctlrn.html">TRCRSCTLR&lt;a&gt;</a>.GROUP == <span class="binarynumber">0b0000</span> and <a href="ext-trcrsctlrn.html">TRCRSCTLR&lt;a&gt;</a>.EXTIN[n] == 1.</p>

      
        <p>If the trace unit is not in the Idle state it is <span class="arm-defined-word">CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE</span> whether writes to this register are ignored.</p>
      <h4>TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt; can be accessed through the external debug interface:</h4><table class="info"><tr><th>Component</th><th>Offset</th><th>Instance</th></tr><tr><td>ETE</td><td><span class="hexnumber">0x120</span> + (4 * n)</td><td>TRCEXTINSELR&lt;n&gt;</td></tr></table><p>Accessible as follows:</p><ul><li>When OSLockStatus(), or !AllowExternalTraceAccess(addrdesc), or !IsTraceCorePowered(), accesses to this register generate an error response.
          </li><li>When n &gt;= NUM_TRACE_EXTERNAL_INPUT_SELECTOR_RESOURCES, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RES0</span>.
          </li><li>Otherwise, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
          </li></ul><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
